     "design": {
      "purpose": "Subtract two-digit numbers within 100, trading 1 ten for 10 ones.",
      "principles": [
       "PRINCIPLE_WORKED_EXAMPLE",
       "PRINCIPLE_RETRIEVAL_PRACTICE"
      ],
      "rationale": "Every item needs a trade in the ones column, so students decide when to regroup only by looking at the digits. The worked example names the trade as 1 ten for 10 ones, which is the place-value reason for crossing out and rewriting digits.",
      "misconceptions": [
       "Subtracting the smaller digit from the larger in each column, whichever is on top: 52 − 38 = 26.",
       "Taking 1 ten from the tens column without adding 10 to the ones."
      ],
      "references": [
       "Common Core Standards Writing Team (2015), Progressions for the Common Core State Standards in Mathematics, Number and Operations in Base Ten, K-5"
